1.  Installation .........................................................

    To install TLXTW Scripts, create a directory on your disk where you
    want to install the scripts.  Extract the archive (TLXTW2xx.ARJ) to
    that directory. Run SETUP.EXE.  Setup will create a batch file called
    TL.BAT and configure certain scripts and compile them.  Now type TL to
    load Telix.

2.  Environment Variables ................................................

    The directory where Telix.exe resides should always be set in the
    environment whether you're using the scripts or not.  See section 1.5
    of Telix.doc for more information about the Telix Environment variable.

    From the Dos Prompt type:  Set Telix=C:\Telix
    (or whatever directory Telix.exe is in).

    Three other environment variables must be set for these scripts.

    F1, DR, and TEMP.

    F1  -  The path where scripts will make and store data files.
           This directory must already exist.
           Ex:  SET F1=C:\Telix\Twgames

    DR  -  Is the delay rate.  If your modem is 9600 bps or faster, this can
           be 1. if you running at 2400 bps, set this to 3 or higher.
           The lower this number the faster Telix responds.  But if it is
           to low, Telix responds to quick.  If your experiencing trouble
           at 2400 bps such as scripts hanging try raising this number
           gradually until the problem disappears, but I wouldn't recommend
           raising it higher than 10.  Unless you want to have to wait for
           a full second in some places. Ex:  SET DR=3

    TEMP  -  where temporary files are stored.
             Ex:  SET Temp=C:\Temp

    Here is an example batch file which loads Telix.

    TEL.BAT
    @echo off
    set telix=c:\telix
    set f1=c:\games\traders
    set dr=4
    set temp=c:\temp
    c:
    cd\telix
    telix
    rem Erase variables when finished
    set f1=
    set dr=

    If any one of the above environment variables is not set, some scripts
    will not function.

    Setup.exe will automatically create TL.BAT.

3.  Configuration File - Tlxtw.Cfg .......................................

    TLXTW.CFG is the configuration file.  Run Config.slc (Alt-E) to edit
    the values in this file.  If you have registered TLXTW2xx Scripts,
    run Config and type "R", then enter your name and registration code
    from your registration letter.

4.  .Key files ...........................................................

    Key files allow you to redefine the keyboard to do things like send
    your name, password, or run scripts, etc, with just the touch of a key.

    The default .key file is Telix.key.

    After Trader.key or Planet.key has been loaded type Alt-F2 to switch
    between the two.  Trader.key is automatically loaded if you start Telix
    via the TL.BAT the Setup.exe creates.

    Please read the Telix documentation for further information about Telix.

