TRADER.KEY  n/a keyboard template.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRANSMIT.SLC    Alt-F4          Trader.key

    Transmits messages to other traders, entire corps, or any combination
    of the two.  Reads the file Transmit.txt from the game's directory.
    This script is mostly so I can write messages to other traders
    offline, then send them while online.

    The format of Transmit.txt is very particular.

    >Phil Crown
    Hello!  interesting stuff...interesting stuff... interesting stuff...
    interesting stuff... interesting stuff... interesting stuff...
    interesting stuff... interesting stuff... interesting stuff...
    interesting stuff... interesting stuff... interesting stuff...
    interesting stuff... interesting stuff... interesting stuff...
    interesting stuff... interesting stuff... interesting stuff...
    interesting stuff... interesting stuff... interesting stuff...

    >Player 2
    same as above ... no limit on the size of the message.

    >end

    The last ">end" is VERY important.  DO NOT use ">" anywhere else in
    the text except as shown above or the script will get lost.
    NOTE:  There should be ONE blank line between each ">" symbol.
    Just format your transmit.txt like the above, and it should be ok.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRANSTEL.SLC    F4          Trader.key

    Runs the Transport/Steal/Sell cycle.  Set up both ships in the sectors
    that you want to steal/sell from with the both ships' holds full.
    Hit F4, enter the ship number you're currently in, the product you want
    to steal from this port, repeat for the second ship, and the rest is
    automatic.  The script begins by transporting to the Ship 2, sells,
    steals, transport to ship 1, sells, steals, Ship2, sell, steal, etc...

    If you get busted, Busted (Alt-F10) is called which records the bust in
    the .bus file.  If you get busted after you abort the script, you will
    have to run Alt-F10 to record the bust in the .bus file.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRICRON.SLC     Ctrl-T      Trader.key

    Plays Tricron for three minutes or until the jackpot is won.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRIPLE.SLC      F5      Trader.key

    Trades three commodities at paired ports.  One port is selling
    two commodities and buying one and the other port is buying the two
    and selling the opposite of the first port.  Except for a Class 7 and
    a Class 8/9, then one port is selling all three and the other port is
    buying all three.

    It works out as follows:

                BBS  1  ³   BSB  2  ³   SBB  3  ³ SSS  7
                SSB  4  ³   SBS  5  ³   BSS  6  ³ BBB  8 or 9

    If you're lucky enough to find a pair of these; fill your holds, be
    ready to move into the adjacent sector to sell, then just hit F5,
    and the rest is automatic. The advantage of trading at a pair of
    these is you have 6 chances of making experience points from haggling
    prices, rather than the standard 4 at normal paired ports.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TWACIMUP.SLC    Alt-F3      Trader.key

